climbT -- the parent chain after layout (SEQ 652, Tony's stroke 1 of the styles build, 2026-11-14).
A field three levels down must climb to its own laid-out parents: text properties are inherited by that climb (drawText).
Before the fix a field under a member of a field written down or across climbed to its old parent, then to fillDownAcross's
scratch list newStuff, and never reached the top: the cause of the seal 451 issue (font not inherited three levels down).
CL-0 is the control on the definition, never laid out. CL-1 a down parent, CL-2 an across parent.
CL-3 to CL-5 (SEQ 653, stroke 2b): a parent that repeats its members, down=3 (clNum) and down="*" (clStar). The repeats are deep
copies added to the field itself: each climbs to the field and the top, each owns its child (the three kids are laid out at y 0, 100
and 200, where the old shallow copies shared one kid, laid out three times at 200), and the parent's style reaches every kid's text.
NOT FIXED, not pinned: a field written both down and across (bothDirections) still rebuilds its list in a scratch field.
